# SEIS-SSH Rule
- Do not include real private keys, hostnames, usernames, or tokens in committed files.
- Do not create or suggest destructive remote commands by default.
- Treat SEIS-SSH as planning/readiness documentation first.
- Any live SSH action must remain approval-gated and explicitly documented.
- Keep deployment/readiness claims tied to evidence, not assumptions.
